    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1384" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδικ-ία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wrongdoing, injustice</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδικίης ἄρχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.130
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				4.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				477c
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύχἡ μᾶλλον ἢ ἀδικίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					6.1
				</span></i>
			; <i>'foul'</i> in racing, <i><span class="en">
				Anon.
				<u>in SE</u>
				30.15
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>wrongful act, offence</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.136
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταγνόντες αὑτῶν ἀδικίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					1.3
				</span></i>
			:—in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				82a
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
